A||N||3||Haze_Performance||Where to find cool Fiero books??||||14||
Z||000000||Haze_Performance||03-06-2001||11:58 AM||||Well I picked up a few Fiero books yesterday.<P>1. Fiero Press Guide 1984/1988 (Hardcover)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/50915.gif"> <BR>Info: This limited edition 320 page press guide contains uncut press material for every Fiero produced. In addition to many photos and diagrams, you will find press releases detailing Fieros of all years, makes and models. The Fiero Press Guide comes in a hard cover, 8 1/2 X 11 format. <P>2. BROOKLAND'S PERFORMANCE PORTFOLIO <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/50209.jpg"> <BR>Info: Contains all of the original articles and testing on the Fiero by major automobile magazines. Newly reprinted from the Road Test book, this new publication has 35 more fact filled pages of Fiero fun. <P>-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<P>I know of the FIERO HISTORY BOOK. Im picking up that one next. Where can I find more books about the Fiero? Im looking for some good Indy pics and info, Mera, SD4, IMSA....ect. Even stock stuff.  <P>TFTS  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Carl<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">  </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>PFF Members Photo Page</A><BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1431213" TARGET=_blank><BR>Photopoint Gallery (Updated Weekly)</A>||||reg||14
Z||000001||Standard||03-06-2001||12:21 PM||||Did you get those from the Fiero Store?  That's the only place I know of to get any Fiero reading material..||||reg||1
